 "details": {
  "title": "I Fall in Love Too Easily",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows Johnny Hartman’s record in his key, B♭ (C for the trumpet), concert A3 to D♭5: the first half free, then the whole song in time at about 65, the second half again and a tag. It keeps his way with it where the page names his notes: A held for two bars, the line two beats behind the band after it, D left hanging over F6, his long F♯ over A6, G over A♭ over C, his last B♭ on top of A♭13. Over the guitar’s C minor 9 the turn takes B♭. It plays in the guitar track’s own beat times, so the free bars stretch with him, and it closes over G♭ major 7, landing on A, the major 7th of B♭.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Jule Styne and Sammy Cahn (1944)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune from the lead sheet, with Hartman’s notes and timing where the Fret Finder page names them, on that page’s chords"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "B♭ major concert (C for the trumpet), Hartman’s key"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Intro, the first half sung freely, the song in time, the second half again, tag, ending"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (ifilte-guitar.mp3), 2:27"
   ],
   [
    "Bars",
    "The page numbers its bars I1 and R1 to R7 before bar 1, so its bar 1 is bar 9 here"
   ]
  ]
 }
